Feature: Architectural Guard Linting in CLI Doctor
  As a developer or CI pipeline maintainer
  I want `kmp doctor --architecture` and `kmp analyze --rules` to detect architectural drift
  So that code generated by AI agents or team members strictly obeys Clean Architecture and KMP boundaries

  Scenario: Detect direct data layer imports in Compose UI presentation components
    Given a Compose Multiplatform UI file inside `src/commonMain/kotlin/.../presentation/`
    When the file contains an import referencing a data repository implementation or DAO
    Then `kmp doctor --architecture` flags a high-severity violation
    And suggests injecting the domain interface via ViewModel instead

  Scenario: Enforce MVI state flow contract on ViewModels exposing mutable state
    Given a ViewModel class in a presentation module
    When the ViewModel exposes a `MutableStateFlow` directly to the public API
    Then `kmp doctor --architecture` flags a rule violation
    And indicates that state must be exposed as read-only `StateFlow` via `asStateFlow()`

  Scenario: Audit module.yaml dependencies against actual code imports
    Given a multiplatform module configured with `module.yaml`
    When an unused dependency coordinate is declared or an undeclared library is imported
    Then `kmp analyze --rules` reports the discrepancy with exact lines
    And exits with non-zero code in CI mode

  Scenario: Run architectural lint via kmp doctor --architecture in CI pipelines
    Given a CI workflow executing `kmp doctor --architecture --json`
    When architectural violations exist
    Then the command outputs structured JSON reporting rule ID, file path, line number, and remediation
    And exits with code 1 to block PR merge
